# USER.md seed

This file is a format for the generated child profile at `$HERMES_HOME/memories/USER.md`. Do not put real child or family data in this repository.

The parent must review every entry. Keep the result compact because Hermes applies a character limit.

Use declarative facts, not instructions to the agent. Put behavior rules in `SOUL.md`.

```text
[CHILD DISPLAY NAME OR PARENT-APPROVED REFERENCE] is in the [AGE OR DEVELOPMENTAL BAND] range.
§
[CHILD] prefers [COMMUNICATION STYLE, ANSWER LENGTH, HUMOR, EMOJI, OR CORRECTION PREFERENCES].
§
[CHILD] learns best through [APPROVED LEARNING PREFERENCES].
§
[CHILD]'s durable interests include [APPROVED INTERESTS].
§
[APPROVED FAMILY OR RELATIONSHIP CONTEXT THAT IMPROVES HELP]. Treat this as private family information.
§
[APPROVED ACCESSIBILITY, LANGUAGE, OR SUPPORT NEEDS STATED AS FACTS, NOT DIAGNOSES INFERRED BY THE AGENT].
```

## Include only when useful

- stable communication preferences;
- durable interests;
- learning preferences;
- parent-approved family terminology;
- accessibility or language needs;
- practical context that improves recurring help.

## Usually exclude

- credentials or account details;
- precise home, school, or routine locations without a clear recurring need;
- moment-by-moment schedules or movements;
- private third-party information;
- temporary moods;
- inferred diagnoses or personality labels;
- crisis disclosures;
- raw conversation history;
- anything the child or parent asked the agent to forget.

Some families may approve precise school, location, or schedule details for a private profile because they materially improve practical help. Treat that as an explicit parent decision, not a default. Document who may receive the information and which external tools or providers may process it.
